    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356">

                <pb facs="1065" n="1059" xml:id="pg1059"/>

                <head>No. 9.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stevens to Mr. Cleghorn.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-01-17"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Yours of the 16th, yesterday, regarding the
                    landing of the United States naval forces in Honolulu, is received. I have
                    carefully considered its import. My responsibility as the United States minister
                    plenipotentiary at this critical time in Hawaiian affairs it is impossible for
                    me to ignore. I assure you that whatever responsibility the American diplomatic
                    and naval representatives have assumed or may assume, we shall do our utmost to
                    regard the welfare of all persons and interests concerned.</p>
                <p>Yours, sincerely, and with the kindest consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John L. Stevens.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. A. S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cleghorn</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Governor of Oahu.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
